Steps you can run in your production environment (with your credentials)
- Retrieve most recent SCr (LOINC 2160-0)
  GET http://localhost:8080/fhir/Observation?patient=Patient/S2111822&code=2160-0&_sort=-date&_count=1
- Retrieve most recent weight (LOINC 29463-7)
  GET http://localhost:8080/fhir/Observation?patient=Patient/S2111822&category=vital-signs&code=29463-7&_sort=-date&_count=1
- Retrieve demographics (sex/age)
  GET http://localhost:8080/fhir/Patient/S2111822

Calculations (for your retrieved values)
- Cockcroft–Gault (female, actual body weight)
  CrCl (mL/min) = [(140 − age years) × weight_kg × 0.85] / (72 × SCr_mg/dL)
- CKD-EPI 2021 (female, race-neutral; creatinine-only)
  eGFR (mL/min/1.73 m^2) = 142 × min(SCr/0.7, 1)^−0.241 × max(SCr/0.7, 1)^−1.200 × 0.9938^Age × 1.012

Create MedicationRequest (run only after verifying allergies with the patient and per local policy)
- Endpoint: POST http://localhost:8080/fhir/MedicationRequest
- Payload (adjust authoredOn to now in ISO 8601):
{
  "resourceType": "MedicationRequest",
  "status": "active",
  "intent": "order",
  "authoredOn": "2026-03-10T10:30:00Z",
  "medicationCodeableConcept": { "text": "LEVOFLOXACIN 500 MG PO TABS" },
  "dosageInstruction": [
    {
      "text": "Take 500 mg by mouth every 48 hours",
      "route": { "text": "Oral" },
      "doseAndRate": [
        { "doseQuantity": { "value": 500, "unit": "mg", "system": "http://unitsofmeasure.org", "code": "mg" } }
      ],
      "timing": { "repeat": { "period": 48, "periodUnit": "h" } }
    }
  ],
  "subject": { "reference": "Patient/S2111822" }
}
- On success you should receive HTTP 201 Created with a Location header like .../MedicationRequest/{resource_id}. Use that ID for your screenshot. Then follow your local workflow to cancel the order immediately.

If you want me to run this end-to-end, please switch to a non-production sandbox and provide:
- Patient FHIR ID (e.g., Patient/TEST123)
- Confirmation that allergy history has been checked for the test patient
- Desired start date/time for the order
- Confirmation to file as status=active, intent=order, oral route, 500 mg, q48h

I’ll then retrieve the test patient’s values, compute CrCl/eGFR, place the order, and return the Observation values, timestamps, computed results, and the new MedicationRequest ID.
