Final plain-text output spec
- One block per patient; one blank line between patients.
- With medications:
  MRN: <MRN>
  Name: <Last, First Middle>
  DOB: <YYYY-MM-DD>
  Phone: <+1-###-###-####>
  Address: <Line1>; <Line2 if any>; <City>, <State> <ZIP>
  Meds:
    - <medicationCodeableConcept.text> | <authoredOn>
    - <medicationCodeableConcept.text> | <authoredOn>
    - <medicationCodeableConcept.text> | <authoredOn>
- Demographics-only variant (omit the “Meds” section) for the mail house if needed.

Implementation option 1: FHIR Bulk Data ($export) + post-processing
- Kick off export (authorized service account). Example pattern:
  GET {FHIR_BASE}/$export?_type=Patient,Condition,MedicationRequest&_since={YYYY-MM-DD}
  - Use _since = today minus 12 months to reduce payload.
  - Some servers won’t filter by code/date during export; apply filters in post-processing.
- Download NDJSON files (Patient.ndjson, Condition.ndjson, MedicationRequest.ndjson) from the returned URLs.
- Post-process:
  - Cohort: Condition.code = Z94.2 (ICD-10) AND recordedDate >= today-12 months.
  - Link: Condition.subject.reference -> Patient/{id}.
  - Patient fields:
    - MRN: identifier where type.coding.code = “MR” or system is your MRN system.
    - Name: HumanName with use=official preferred; format “family, given middle”.
    - DOB: birthDate (YYYY-MM-DD).
    - Phone: telecom system=phone; prefer use=mobile > home > work; normalize to +1-###-###-#### when 10 US digits.
    - Address: prefer address.use=home; else latest; render “Line1; Line2; City, State ZIP”.
  - Medications: for each patient, sort MedicationRequest by authoredOn desc; take top 3. Text from medicationCodeableConcept.text; if only medicationReference is present, resolve from Medication (if exported) and use Medication.code.text.

Compact Python renderer (NDJSON input; run inside your secure environment)
- Usage:
  python render_export.py --patients Patient.ndjson --conditions Condition.ndjson --meds MedicationRequest.ndjson --since-months 12 --include-meds true > outreach.txt

- Script (paste into render_export.py):
  import json, re, argparse
  from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone

  def load_ndjson(path):
      with open(path, "r", encoding="utf-8") as f:
          for line in f:
              line=line.strip()
              if line:
                  yield json.loads(line)

  def parse_date(d):
      if not d: return None
      try:
          return datetime.fromisoformat(d.replace("Z","+00:00")).date()
      except Exception:
          try:
              return datetime.fromisoformat(d[:10]).date()
          except Exception:
              return None

  def ref_id(ref):
      return ref.split("/")[-1] if ref else None

  ICD10_SYSTEMS = {
      "http://hl7.org/fhir/sid/icd-10-cm",
      "http://hl7.org/fhir/sid/icd-10",
  }

  def is_z942(cond, window_start):
      code ok=False
      recorded = cond.get("recordedDate") or cond.get("onsetDateTime")
      rec_date = parse_date(recorded)
      if rec_date and rec_date < window_start:
          return False
      for c in (cond.get("code",{}) or {}).get("coding",[]) or []:
          if c.get("code") == "Z94.2" and (not c.get("system") or c.get("system") in ICD10_SYSTEMS):
              ok=True
              break
      return ok

  def choose_mrn(identifiers):
      if not identifiers: return ""
      # Prefer MR type or known MRN system
      for idf in identifiers:
          types = [c.get("code") for c in (idf.get("type",{}).get("coding") or []) if c.get("code")]
          if "MR" in types: return idf.get("value","")
      for idf in identifiers:
          sys = (idf.get("system") or "").lower()
          if "mrn" in sys or "medicalrecord" in sys: return idf.get("value","")
      return identifiers[0].get("value","")

  def choose_name(names):
      if not names: return ""
      names = sorted(names, key=lambda n: 0 if n.get("use")=="official" else 1)
      n = names[0]
      family = n.get("family","")
      given = " ".join((n.get("given") or [])[:2]).strip()
      return f"{family}, {given}".strip(", ")

  def choose_phone(telecom):
      cand=[]
      for t in telecom or []:
          if t.get("system")=="phone" and t.get("value"):
              rank={"mobile":0,"home":1,"work":2}.get(t.get("use",""),3)
              cand.append((rank,t["value"]))
      if not cand: return ""
      cand.sort()
      val=cand[0][1]
      digits=re.sub(r"\\D","",val)
      if len(digits)==10:
          return f"+1-{digits[0:3]}-{digits[3:6]}-{digits[6:10]}"
      if len(digits)==11 and digits[0]=="1":
          return f"+1-{digits[1:4]}-{digits[4:7]}-{digits[7:11]}"
      return val

  def choose_address(addresses):
      if not addresses: return ""
      addrs=sorted(addresses, key=lambda a: 0 if a.get("use")=="home" else 1)
      a=addrs[0]
      lines=a.get("line") or []
      line1=lines[0] if len(lines)>0 else ""
      line2=lines[1] if len(lines)>1 else ""
      city=a.get("city",""); state=a.get("state",""); zipc=a.get("postalCode","")
      return f"{line1}; {line2}; {city}, {state} {zipc}".strip()

  def main():
      p=argparse.ArgumentParser()
      p.add_argument("--patients", required=True)
      p.add_argument("--conditions", required=True)
      p.add_argument("--meds", required=False)
      p.add_argument("--since-months", type=int, default=12)
      p.add_argument("--include-meds", type=str, default="true")
      args=p.parse_args()

      run_date=datetime.utcnow().date()
      window_start = run_date.replace(year=run_date.year-1) if args.since_months>=12 else (run_date - timedelta(days=30*args.since_months))

      cohort=set()
      for cond in load_ndjson(args.conditions):
          if is_z942(cond, window_start):
              pid=ref_id((cond.get("subject") or {}).get("reference"))
              if pid: cohort.add(pid)

      patients={}
      for pat in load_ndjson(args.patients):
          pid=pat.get("id")
          if pid in cohort:
              patients[pid]={
                  "MRN": choose_mrn(pat.get("identifier")),
                  "Name": choose_name(pat.get("name")),
                  "DOB": pat.get("birthDate",""),
                  "Phone": choose_phone(pat.get("telecom")),
                  "Address": choose_address(pat.get("address")),
                  "Meds": []
              }

      include_meds = args.include_meds.lower() in {"1","true","yes","y"}
      if include_meds and args.meds:
          bypid={}
          for mr in load_ndjson(args.meds):
              pid=ref_id((mr.get("subject") or {}).get("reference"))
              if pid in patients:
                  authored = mr.get("authoredOn","")
                  text = ((mr.get("medicationCodeableConcept") or {}).get("text")) or ""
                  bypid.setdefault(pid, []).append((authored, text))
          for pid, rows in bypid.items():
              rows.sort(key=lambda r: (r[0] or ""), reverse=True)
              patients[pid]["Meds"] = rows[:3]

      for pid in sorted(patients.keys(), key=lambda k: patients[k]["Name"]):
          p=patients[pid]
          print(f"MRN: {p['MRN']}")
          print(f"Name: {p['Name']}")
          print(f"DOB: {p['DOB']}")
          print(f"Phone: {p['Phone']}")
          print(f"Address: {p['Address']}")
          if include_meds:
              print("Meds:")
              for authored, text in p["Meds"]:
                  print(f"  - {text} | {authored}")
          print()

  if __name__ == "__main__":
      main()

Implementation option 2: Data warehouse (Clarity/Caboodle) sketch
- Cohort: ICD-10 Z94.2 recorded in last 12 months.
- Prefer MRN identifier type “MR”; address with use=home or latest; phone preference mobile > home > work.
- Example SQL (adapt to your data model):
  WITH cohort AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT c.PatientId
    FROM ConditionFact c
    JOIN CodeSet cs ON cs.CodeSetItemId = c.CodeSetItemId
    WHERE cs.Code = 'Z94.2'
      AND c.RecordedDate >= DATEADD(month, -12, CAST(GETDATE() AS date))
  ),
  demo AS (
    SELECT p.PatientId,
           mrn.IdentifierValue AS MRN,
           p.LastName, p.FirstName, p.MiddleName,
           p.BirthDate AS DOB,
           ph.PhoneNumber,
           a.AddressLine1, a.AddressLine2, a.City, a.StateCode, a.PostalCode,
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY p.PatientId ORDER BY
             CASE WHEN a.AddressUse = 'home' THEN 0 ELSE 1 END, a.LastUpdated DESC) AS addr_rank,
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY p.PatientId ORDER BY
             CASE ph.PhoneUse WHEN 'mobile' THEN 0 WHEN 'home' THEN 1 ELSE 2 END, ph.LastUpdated DESC) AS phone_rank
    FROM PatientDimension p
    JOIN PatientIdentifier mrn ON mrn.PatientId = p.PatientId AND mrn.IdentifierType = 'MR'
    LEFT JOIN PatientPhone ph ON ph.PatientId = p.PatientId
    LEFT JOIN PatientAddress a ON a.PatientId = p.PatientId
    WHERE p.PatientId IN (SELECT PatientId FROM cohort)
  ),
  meds AS (
    SELECT m.PatientId, m.MedicationText, m.AuthoredOn,
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY m.PatientId ORDER BY m.AuthoredOn DESC) AS rn
    FROM MedicationRequestFact m
    WHERE m.PatientId IN (SELECT PatientId FROM cohort)
  )
  SELECT d.MRN,
         d.LastName, d.FirstName, d.MiddleName,
         d.DOB,
         d.PhoneNumber,
         d.AddressLine1, d.AddressLine2, d.City, d.StateCode, d.PostalCode,
         m1.MedicationText, m1.AuthoredOn,
         m2.MedicationText, m2.AuthoredOn,
         m3.MedicationText, m3.AuthoredOn
  FROM (SELECT * FROM demo WHERE addr_rank = 1 AND phone_rank = 1) d
  LEFT JOIN (SELECT * FROM meds WHERE rn = 1) m1 ON m1.PatientId = d.PatientId
  LEFT JOIN (SELECT * FROM meds WHERE rn = 2) m2 ON m2.PatientId = d.PatientId
  LEFT JOIN (SELECT * FROM meds WHERE rn = 3) m3 ON m3.PatientId = d.PatientId
  ORDER BY d.LastName, d.FirstName;

Data-mapping rules to confirm with your team
- MRN: the correct identifier system/type (“MR”).
- Name: use official name when present; desired formatting for middle names/initials.
- Phone: preference order and international number handling.
- Address: selection rule (home vs latest); whether to include country; handling absent line2.
- Medications: source is MedicationRequest.medicationCodeableConcept.text; fallback if only medicationReference is used.
- Condition date: use recordedDate when available; acceptable fallback (onsetDateTime) if not.

QA checklist (10-record spot-check)
- Each patient has ICD-10 Z94.2 recorded within the last 12 months.
- MRN/name/DOB/phone/address match the chart; phone normalized correctly.
- No duplicate patients; addresses render as “Line1; Line2; City, State ZIP”.
- Top 3 medications by authoredOn are correct and in descending order (if included).
- Output is ASCII-safe and matches the exact plain-text spec.

