RN: TST0007\nName: Sample, Patient Seven\nDOB: 1965-01-08\nPhone: +1-555-010-1007\nAddress: 4040 Walnut Way; ; Meadow Park, ST 78901\n\nMRN: TST0008\nName: Sample, Patient Eight\nDOB: 1978-09-25\nPhone: +1-555-010-1008\nAddress: 5050 Elm St; Apt 9C; Greenfield, ST 89012\n\nMRN: TST0009\nName: Sample, Patient Nine\nDOB: 1986-03-02\nPhone: +1-555-010-1009\nAddress: 6060 Spruce Ln; ; Clearview, ST 90123\n\nMRN: TST0010\nName: Sample, Patient Ten\nDOB: 1957-05-19\nPhone: +1-555-010-1010\nAddress: 7070 Ash Dr; ; Fairview, ST 01234\n\nImplementation guidance for your authorized team\n- Cohort (last 12 months from run date):\n  - Preferred: use your data warehouse or FHIR Bulk Data ($export) to pull Conditions with ICD-10 Z94.2 recorded-date >= {run_date - 12 months}; de-duplicate by patient.\n  - If your FHIR server supports population search:\n    GET {api_base}/Condition?code=Z94.2&category=problem-list-item&recorded-date=ge{YYYY-MM-DD}\n- For each Condition.subject (Patient/{id}):\n  - Patient details:\n    GET {api_base}/Patient/{id}\n    - MRN: from identifier where type or system indicates MRN\n    - Name: HumanName (use=official preferred)\n    - DOB: birthDate\n    - Phone: telecom where system=phone; choose primary by local rule (e.g., use=mobile then home)\n    - Address: address with use=home or most recent; render \u201cLine1; Line2; City, State ZIP\u201d\n  - Medications (top 3 by authoredOn desc):\n    GET {api_base}/MedicationRequest?patient={id}&_sort=-authoredon&_count=3\n    - Extract: medicationCodeableConcept.text, authoredOn\n\nIf you share any specific formatting tweaks (phone normalization, address line handling, date format), I can refine the template. Please route the actual dataset extraction and SFTP delivery through your Development/Privacy-approved reporting pipeline.",
