      "content": "Great\u2014glad the parser validated against the synthetic sample. I won\u2019t retrieve or disclose PHI here. Below are optional hardening add-ons you can drop into your secure environment renderer so you can produce local QA previews (tokenized/redacted) and alternate output formats without changing the core cohort logic.\n\nRenderer add-ons (drop-in updates)\n- New CLI flags\n  - --csv: output CSV instead of plain text\n  - --phone-format {plus1dashes,e164}: choose +1-###-###-#### (default) or E.164 (+1XXXXXXXXXX for US 10/11-digit numbers)\n  - --address-selection {home_or_latest,latest}: keep current home-first logic (default) or force most-recent address\n  - --tokenize-mrn: replace MRN with stable token (SHA256(mrn)[:8], uppercase)\n  - --redact: redact fields for QA previews (never export outside secure env)\n    - Redacts Name and Address lines with placeholders but preserves separators and city/state/ZIP shape\n  - --redact-fixed-len N: placeholder length for redacted text (default 4, renders \u201c\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u201d)\n\n- Imports to add at top\n  - import hashlib, csv\n\n- Helper additions\n  - MRN tokenization:\n    def tokenize_mrn(mrn):\n        if not mrn: return \"\"\n        return hashlib.sha256(mrn.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()[:8].upper()\n  - Redaction helpers (fixed-length placeholder, preserve city/state/ZIP shape):\n    def placeholder(n=4, ch=\"\u2588\"):\n        return ch * max(1, n)\n    def redact_name(name, n=4):\n        # Keep comma/space separators; mask tokens\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in name.split(\",\")]\n        if len(parts) == 2:\n            family = placeholder(n); given = placeholder(n)\n            return f\"{family}, {given}\"\n        return placeholder(n)\n    def split_address(addr):\n        # \u201cLine1; Line2; City, ST ZIP\u201d -> (line1, line2, city, state, zip)\n        try:\n            line_part, cityst = addr.split(\"; ; \")[0:2] if \"; ; \" in addr else addr.split(\";\", 2)[0:2]\n        except ValueError:\n            parts = addr.split(\";\")\n            parts += [\"\"]*(3-len(parts))\n            line_part, line2 = parts[0].strip(), parts[1].strip() if len(parts)>1 else \"\"\n            city, state_zip = (\"\", \"\")\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in addr.split(\";\")]\n        line1 = parts[0] if len(parts)>0 else \"\"\n        line2 = parts[1] if len(parts)>1 else \"\"\n        tail = parts[2] if len(parts)>2 else \"\"\n        if \", \" in tail:\n            city, rest = tail.split(\", \", 1)\n        else:\n            city, rest = \"\", tail\n        st, zipc = (rest.split(\" \", 1)+[\"\"])[:2] if rest else (\"\",\"\")\n        return line1, line2, city, st, zipc\n    def redact_address(addr, n=4):\n        l1, l2, city, st, zipc = split_address(addr)\n        # Replace line1/line2 with fixed placeholders; keep city/state/ZIP shape but substitute synthetic values\n        rl1 = placeholder(n); rl2 = placeholder(n) if l2 else \"\"\n        rcity = \"City\" if city else \"\"\n        rst = (st[:2].upper() if st else \"ST\")\n        rzip = \"12345-6789\" if \"-\" in (zipc or \"\") else (\"12345\" if zipc else \"\")\n        return f\"{rl1}; {rl2}; {rcity}, {rst} {rzip}\".strip()\n  - E.164 switch and address-selection switch:\n    def format_phone_e164(digits):\n        # US-only: 10 or 11-digit (leading 1) to +1XXXXXXXXXX; else return original\n        if len(digits)==10: return f\"+1{digits}\"\n        if len(digits)==11 and digits[0]==\"1\": return f\"+1{digits[1:]}\"\n        return None\n    # In choose_phone(), if args.phone_format == \"e164\", apply format_phone_e164 and fall back to original if not applicable.\n    # For address selection, add a flag to bypass \u201chome\u201d preference and sort strictly by recency:\n    def address_rank_latest(addr):\n        per = addr.get(\"period\") or {}\n        end = parse_date(per.get(\"end\"))\n        start = parse_date(per.get(\"start\"))\n        # Newest first\n        return (-(end.toordinal() if end else -10**9), -(start.toordinal() if start else -10**9))\n\n- Hook-ups in argument parser\n  - ap.add_argument(\"--csv\", action=\"store_true\")\n  - ap.add_argument(\"--phone-format\", choices=[\"plus1dashes\",\"e164\"], default=\"plus1dashes\")\n  - ap.add_argument(\"--address-selection\", choices=[\"home_or_latest\",\"latest\"], default=\"home_or_latest\")\n  - ap.add_argument(\"--tokenize-mrn\", action=\"store_true\")\n  - ap.add_argument(\"--redact\", action=\"store_true\")\n  - ap.add_argument(\"--redact-fixed-len\", type=int, default=4)\n\n- Where you build patient dict\n  - If args.tokenize_mrn: mrn = tokenize_mrn(mrn)\n  - If args.redact: name_fmt = redact_name(name_fmt, args.redact_fixed_len)\n  - If args.redact: addr = redact_address(addr, args.redact_fixed_len)\n\n- In choose_address()\n  - If args.address_selection == \"latest\": sort addresses with address_rank_latest instead of use=home logic.\n\n- In choose_phone()\n  - After selecting the best number, normalize digits and:\n    - if args.phone_format == \"e164\": try format_phone_e164(digits); if None, leave original\n    - else use existing +1-###-###-#### formatting\n\n- CSV output mode\n  - If args.csv, write rows using Python\u2019s csv module with header:\n    MRN,Name,DOB,Phone,AddressLine1,AddressLine2,City,State,ZIP[,Med1,Med1Date,Med2,Med2Date,Med3,Med3Date]\n  - To support this, split the address into its components (using split_address) before writing.\n\nExample commands (inside your secure environment)\n- Demographics-only, plain text, redacted QA preview with tokenized MRNs:\n  python3 render_outreach.py --patients Patient.ndjson --conditions Condition.ndjson --demographics-only --tokenize-mrn --redact --redact-fixed-len 6 --ascii-only > preview_redacted.txt\n- Full output with meds, E.164 phones, and \u201clatest\u201d address policy, CSV:\n  python3 render_outreach.py --patients Patient.ndjson --conditions Condition.ndjson --medreq MedicationRequ