      "content": "I can\u2019t access or use patient PHI or place orders in a live chart for a non-care/training purpose. That includes retrieving data or creating a MedicationRequest for Valerie Young. This protects patient privacy and prevents non-care entries in production records.\n\nSafe ways to complete your demo today\n- Best option: Use a designated test/sandbox environment and a non-real \u201cTraining/Test\u201d patient. If you provide the test patient\u2019s FHIR ID, I can run the full workflow (retrieve values, do the calculations, and create the order) there.\n- Alternative: I can do a full mock walkthrough with de-identified synthetic inputs and show the exact API calls and payloads you would run, without touching real PHI or live charts.\n\nIf you can switch to a test patient, please provide:\n- Patient FHIR ID (e.g., Patient/TEST123)\n- Confirmation that this is in a non-production training environment\n- Confirmation that allergy history has been checked for the test patient (required before posting a MedicationRequest)\n- Start date/time for the order (e.g., today at 10:30 local)\n- OK to file as \u201cactive, intent=order,\u201d timing q48h, oral route, 500 mg dose\n\nWhat I can provide right now (de-identified demo content)\n1) How to retrieve the needed data\n- Most recent serum creatinine (LOINC 2160-0):\n  GET {base}/Observation?patient=Patient/{TEST_ID}&code=2160-0&_sort=-date&_count=1\n- Most recent body weight (LOINC 29463-7) from vitals:\n  GET {base}/Observation?patient=Patient/{TEST_ID}&category=vital-signs\n  Then client-filter for code 29463-7 (Body weight) and take the most recent. If your system supports code on vitals:\n  GET {base}/Observation?patient=Patient/{TEST_ID}&category=vital-signs&code=29463-7&_sort=-date&_count=1\n- Patient demographics (age/sex):\n  GET {base}/Patient?identifier={YOUR_TEST_PATIENT_IDENTIFIER}\n  or if you already have the FHIR ID:\n  GET {base}/Patient/{TEST_ID}\n\n2) Calculations (use these with your re