0 SBP or >90 DBP). No active antihypertensive on file. No new antihypertensive order drafted.\u201d\n\nNotes on identifiers in the Observation.note:\n- To follow minimum-necessary use, I\u2019ve limited the note to name, DOB, and MRN. Phone number and full home address are typically not required within a vitals Observation note for care coordination. If you believe including phone/address is necessary for this care handoff, please explicitly confirm and I can include:\n  - Phone (from chart)\n  - Full home address (from chart)\n\nPlease review and confirm next steps:\n1) File the Observation above as-is? If you want phone/address appended to the note, confirm that inclusion is necessary for this care task and I\u2019ll add them.\n2) Do you want me to draft a lisinopril 10 mg PO daily MedicationRequest despite the average being below your treatment threshold? If yes, I\u2019ll prepare a draft with:\n   - status: active, intent: order\n   - medicationCodeableConcept.text: \u201clisinopril 10 mg tablet\u201d\n   - dosageInstruction: route Oral; timing \u201cEvery day\u201d; dose 10 mg\n   - authoredOn: now\n   - subject.reference: Patient/S2090974\n   (You already attested allergy/contraindication checks.)\n\nI will not post any changes until you confirm.",
