      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. Please help with the following for patient Jonathan Jackson (MRN S1733937, DOB 1984-11-03):\n\n1) Retrieve blood pressures\n- Pull the last three BP Observations. If fewer than three are available, use whatever is available within the past 48 hours.\n- Use LOINC codes if needed: panel 85354-9, SBP 8480-6, DBP 8462-4.\n- Return the Observation IDs, timestamps, and SBP/DBP values.\n\n2) Compute averages\n- Calculate the average SBP and average DBP from the retrieved Observations.\n- Report the averages.\n\n3) Check current antihypertensives\n- Review active MedicationRequests to determine whether an ACE inhibitor or ARB is currently active.\n- If one is active, identify the medication name and status.\n\n4) Conditional order placement\n- If NO active ACE inhibitor or ARB is found AND the average BP meets BOTH thresholds (average SBP \u2265110 and average DBP \u226580), then place a new MedicationRequest from the HTN initiation order set:\n  - Medication: lisinopril 10 mg tablet (RxNorm 314077)\n  - Intent: order\n  - Route: oral\n  - Frequency: daily\n  - Quantity: per local default\n  - Reason code/diagnosis: essential hypertension (ICD-10 I10)\n  - authoredOn: set to the current UTC timestamp (do not backdate; if backdating is ever considered, include a clear rationale per policy and only proceed with explicit instruction)\n- Safety checks: If there is a documented ACE inhibitor allergy, prior angioedema, pregnancy, potassium >5.5 mEq/L, or eGFR <30 mL/min/1.73 m\u00b2, do not place the order and report back.\n\n5) Post and summarize\n- Post the order if placed.\n- Return a concise summary including:\n  - The BP Observations used and the calculated average SBP/DBP\n  - Whether an ACEi/ARB is active (and which one, if applicable)\n  - Details of any new MedicationRequest (ID, authoredOn, status) or the reason it was not placed."
    },
