      "content": "Thanks\u2014I'll proceed stepwise and flag anything that blocks the plan.\n\nStep 1) Patient confirmation\n- Found exactly one patient by MRN S3213957.\n- EMR demographics match your provided details:\n  - Name: Tina Reid\n  - DOB: 1953-10-18\n  - Sex: male\n  - MRN (FHIR id): S3213957\nStatus: Complete.\n\nStep 2) Labs/demographics for CrCl\n- Serum creatinine (LOINC 2160-0) within last 72 hours: not found. Query: Observation?code=2160-0&patient=S3213957&date=ge2023-11-10T10:15:00+00:00 returned 0 results.\n- Weight: no weight Observation found. Query: Observation?code=29463-7&patient=S3213957 returned 0 results. Per your instruction, will use actual body weight = 78 kg if/when calculating.\n- Sex: male (from Patient resource).\n- Age today (2023-11-13): 70 years (DOB 1953-10-18).\n\nCreatinine clearance (Cockcroft\u2013Gault)\n- Unable to calculate at this time because no serum creatinine value was found within the last 72 hours. Inputs that would be used if SCr were available:\n  - Age: 70 years\n  - Sex: male\n  - Weight: 78 kg (actual, per instruction due to no weight Observation)\n  - SCr: not available in past 72 hours (units/time unavailable)\nIf you\u2019d like, I can expand the lab search window or place an order for a serum creatinine per your workflow.\n\nStep 3) Place MedicationRequest (undosed active order for levofloxacin)\nBefore I submit any order, I must restate and get your explicit confirmation:\n- Proposed action: Create an active MedicationRequest with no dosage instructions for levofloxacin, reason \u201cpneumonia due to COVID-19 (ICD-10-CM J12.82),\u201d subject Patient/S3213957 (Tina Reid, DOB 1953-10-18). Include a free-text note \u201cPatient denies medication allergies today.\u201d\n- Allergy history: You noted the patient denies med allergies today.\n\nImportant system constraint:\n- The MedicationRequest.Create endpoint in this environment requires dosageInstruction. Creating an active order without any dosing details will be rejected by the API. This conflicts with \u201cactive, no dosing\u201d as requested.\nOptions to proceed:\nA) Provide minimal dosing instructions (e.g., route and a placeholder frequency/dose per your direction) so I can file an active order now.\nB) Allow me to create a draft/held order without dosing (if acceptable in your workflow), which complies with the API and your intent to let pharmacy complete dosing later.\nC) Alternatively, place a ServiceRequest for \u201cPharmacy to dose levofloxacin for COVID-19 pneumonia\u201d and then convert to a dosed MedicationRequest once pharmacy enters dosing.\n\nProposed MedicationRequest payload (what I would post if the system allowed \u201cactive, no dosing\u201d):\n- Note: RxNorm code lookup isn\u2019t available to me here; I will use the medication text \u201clevofloxacin.\u201d If you supply an RxCUI, I can include it.\n{\n  \"resourceType\": \"MedicationRequest\",\n  \"status\": \"active\",\n  \"intent\": \"order\",\n  \"authoredOn\": \"2023-11-13T10:15:00+00:00\",\n  \"medicationCodeableConcept\": {\n    \"text\": \"levofloxacin\"\n  },\n  \"subject\": { \"reference\": \"Patient/S3213957\" },\n  \"reasonCode\": [\n    {\n      \"coding\": [\n        {\n          \"system\": \"http://hl7.org/fhir/sid/icd-10-cm\",\n          \"code\": \"J12.82\",\n          \"display\": \"Pneumonia due to coronavirus disease 2019\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"text\": \"pneumonia due to COVID-19\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"note\": [\n    { \"text\": \"Patient denies medication allergies today\" }\n  ]\n}\n\nPlease confirm:\n1) Proceed for patient Tina Reid (MRN S3213957, DOB 1953-10-18).\n2) Which option (A, B, or C) should I use given the API requirement for dosageInstruction?\n- If A, please provide the minimal dosing details you want included.\n- If B, I will create a draft MedicationRequest without dosing.\n- If C, I will place a ServiceRequest to pharmacy with the indication and your note.\n\nOnce I have your confirmation and selected option, I\u2019ll submit and return the MedicationRequest (or ServiceRequest) ID and the final JSON posted.",
