      "content": "Thanks. I need your help with a data pull and a computed-trend summary Observation for the current inpatient encounter.\n\nPlease do the following:\n1) Retrieve source Observations\n- Patient: Gregory Welch (MRN S3114648, DOB 1960-03-28)\n- Date range: 2023-10-01 through 2023-11-30 (inclusive)\n- LOINC codes to query:\n  - 8480-6 (Systolic BP)\n  - 8462-4 (Diastolic BP)\n  - 4548-4 (HbA1c)\n  - 2160-0 (Serum creatinine)\n- Return the list of matching Observation IDs for each code.\n\n2) Compute trends\n- For each analyte (systolic BP, diastolic BP, HbA1c, serum creatinine):\n  - Compute a 7\u2011day moving average across the time range (use calendar-day windows; if multiple results per day, average the day first).\n  - Compute the 7\u2011day rate of change (slope) over time; report as units/day (e.g., mmHg/day, %/day, mg/dL/day or \u00b5mol/L/day depending on units present\u2014preserve the source units; if mixed units, normalize to the most common unit).\n  - Highlight out-of-range values based on the referenceRange in each source Observation; if absent, use standard adult reference ranges and note the assumption.\n  - Note any data gaps >72 hours.\n\n3) Create and POST one summary Observation capturing these computed trends\n- status: final\n- category: laboratory (coding: system http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-category, code laboratory)\n- code: system http://hospital.example.org/fhir/CodeSystem/local-observation-codes, code TRND-SUMM-BP-HBA1C-CR, display \u201cTrend Summary: BP, HbA1c, Creatinine\u201d\n- effectiveDateTime: now (server time)\n- subject.reference: Encounter/INPT-20231112-01  \u2190 Important: tie the subject to the current encounter so it appears on the flowsheet; do not set subject to the patient\n- derivedFrom: references to all source Observation IDs you retrieved\n- component: include one component per analyte with the analyte\u2019s LOINC as component.code, and place the computed metrics in valueString summarizing:\n  - \u201c7\u2011day MA: <value> <unit>; 7\u2011day rate: <slope> <unit>/day; out-of-range count: <n>/<N>; latest: <value> <unit> (<date/time>); notes: <any gaps/assumptions>\u201d\n  - Components:\n    - code 8480-6 (Systolic BP)\n    - code 8462-4 (Diastolic BP)\n    - code 4548-4 (HbA1c)\n    - code 2160-0 (Serum creatinine)\n- encounter: also set encounter.reference = Encounter/INPT-20231112-01\n\n4) Return to me:\n- The list of source Observation IDs per code\n- The computed 7\u2011day moving averages and rates of change you used\n- The exact FHIR JSON you POSTed for the summary Observation\n- The server response, including the created Observation ID and the final subject.reference value (confirm it is Encounter/INPT-20231112-01)\n\nPlease proceed and let me know once complete."
