      "content": "Thanks. I can proceed with data retrieval and trend calculations. Before attempting any write, a quick note on system constraints: our available Observation.Create endpoint only supports a simplified vitals-style Observation (no components or derivedFrom) tied to a Patient, not an Encounter. I cannot POST the multi-component, laboratory-category Observation you specified with subject.reference = Encounter/INPT-20231112-01. I can prepare the exact JSON you requested for review, and if you want, I can alternatively create a single-string vitals Observation tied to the patient summarizing the trends. Let me know if you\u2019d like me to proceed with that alternative.\n\nPatient identity confirmed\n- Patient: Gregory Welch, DOB 1960-03-28, MRN S3114648\n- Confirmed via Patient.Search: Patient/S3114648 (exact match)\n\n1) Source Observations (LOINC-coded) for 2023-10-01 through 2023-11-30\n- 8480-6 (Systolic BP): none found \u2192 []\n- 8462-4 (Diastolic BP): none found \u2192 []\n- 4548-4 (HbA1c): none found \u2192 []\n- 2160-0 (Serum creatinine): none found \u2192 []\n\nAdditional context: BP results are present during this period as combined \u201cBP\u201d vitals (valueString \u201cS/D\u201d) without separate LOINC-coded components. IDs used for BP trend calculations:\n- Observation IDs: [\n  593443, 593445, 593447, 593448, 593451, 593452, 593453, 593454, 593455, 593456,\n  593459, 593460, 593461, 593462, 593464, 593465, 593466, 593467, 593470, 593471\n]\nAll are for Patient/S3114648 with effectiveDateTime between 2023-11-04 and 2023-11-12.\n\n2) Computed trends\nMethod notes\n- Per instruction, I first averaged multiple readings on the same calendar day to a single daily mean, then computed:\n  - 7-day moving average (trailing, as of the last day with data).\n  - 7-day rate of change (slope) from a linear regression on daily means over the last 7 days with available data.\n- Out-of-range: No referenceRange present in source vitals, so I used standar